  "reason": "Evidence: Our current best (config_041, 0.7250 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion in multiprofile mode. All multiprofile variants with these encoders have been tested, and the improvements from each component are well-characterized. However, singleprofile multimodal with the best encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) is completely untested. This experiment tests whether removing the multiprofile aggregation step (aggregation=None) and fusing the two modalities directly via weighted combination can match or exceed 0.7250. It is the highest-value untested direction: if it succeeds, it may offer a comparable-accuracy, lower-cost alternative (no aggregation step, expected ~3–3.5 GPU hours, slightly cheaper than config_041's 3.60); if it fails, it confirms config_041 as the optimal architecture among available options, allowing the final experiment to focus on a last refinement. With only 2 experiments remaining, resolving this single unexplored architectural axis is the best use of the next slot."
